  "review_decisions": [
    "Elementary exponential, logarithmic, power and trigonometric functions are added because the coordinate and asymptotic formulas use them.",
    "Rectangular left/right inverses are separated from square matrix inversion.",
    "Outer products use a real bilinear convention and explicitly distinguish complex Hermitian covariance.",
    "Absolute value now declares its real-number prerequisite.",
    "Cylindrical differential formulas are derived from the moving orthonormal frame; scalar and vector Laplacians are distinguished.",
    "Axis regularity is a proved sufficient criterion in Cartesian components, not a claim that arbitrary smooth cylindrical components extend.",
    "Vector potential existence is stated on a star-shaped region with an explicit integral construction; compact support is not inferred.",
    "Tensor divergence differentiates the second index, and the streamfunction sign is stated explicitly.",
    "Existing smooth-map, modulus, dyadic-annulus and calculus entries are reused; newly exposed square-root and complex-modulus dependencies are recorded.",
    "Sine and cosine refer to one another only for derived identities; neither definition depends on the other.",
    "The divergence-free condition has its own entry; parity is one reflection-sign classification with its two cases.",
    "Three scope-label findings in pre-existing subject-index rows were inspected and retained as unrelated baseline findings; the added navigation has correct targets.",
    "Integration-simplex and parameter inverse estimates are handled in B03; smooth division and endpoint square-root extension in B04/B09; Gaussian integrals in B07; torus geometry in B08.",
    "The diagonalizability example now correctly says one-dimensional eigenspace instead of only one eigenvector."
  ],
